; c16-four-of-a-suit. Anchor: shot-0233 (Ch. 16, four trumps, a closing aside).
; Printed: 0.28.
; Claim: a freshly drawn seven-tile hand holds four tiles of one pip suit.
; State: none; a uniformly random hand of seven from the 28.
; Exact: 349356/1184040 = 0.2951 for four or more in some suit;
;   317450/1184040 = 0.2681 for a longest suit of exactly four. Ambiguous.
;
; GAP deal-view: a probability over every hand the viewer could be dealt.
;   A Silas frame fixes the viewer's hand and draws only the other three, so
;   the deal itself is not a belief Silas can build. The query below is the
;   event for one known hand (no trump, where a tile follows both of its
;   pips); tests/book_odds.rs checks it hand by hand and computes the whole
;   deal by enumeration in plain Rust.
(query
  (roles (chair v) (context q) (domino a) (domino b) (domino c) (domino d))
  (out)
  (pattern
    (viewer v)
    (not (context q q*))
    (in a q) (in b q) (in c q) (in d q)
    (holds v a) (holds v b) (holds v c) (holds v d)))
